  "objective": "Evaluate web content to determine whether text alternatives are provided for images, video, and other non-text content.",
  "recent_history": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I need to evaluate whether non-text content has good alternatives. I know images sometimes need alt text, but I am not sure how to decide what counts as good or when something should be ignored."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Start with one question: what job is this non-text content doing here? If it communicates information or has a function, a good alternative is text that is programmatically associated with it and serves that same purpose; if it is only decoration, visual formatting, or not meant to be understood by the user, then the right result is usually that assistive technology should ignore it rather than hear extra text. For example, a chart needs text that gives the information it contributes, but a purely decorative divider image should be marked so assistive technology ignores it.\n\nIf you found a leaf-pattern image used only as a visual border, would you judge it by asking \u201cis there a good description?\u201d or by asking \u201cis it hidden from assistive technology?\u201d and why?"
